# {{ site.name }}

> {{ site.name }} is a free, open-source desktop app for transcribing music and learning songs by ear: it slows audio and video down without changing the pitch, shifts the pitch, loops the hard part, marks sections and finds the beats and bars. For Windows, macOS and Linux.

{{ site.name }} is free in full: no trial, no subscription, no paid version, no account, no ads. It is open source under the MIT licence. It runs on your computer and needs the internet only to download from YouTube. It helps a musician work music out by ear; it doesn't transcribe automatically or write out the notes.

